From: BOOKWORM <bookworm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: do not dereference an unpopulated role in cdns_role_stop()

The role switch is registered in cdns_init() before cdns_core_init_role()
fills cdns->roles[]. On CIX Sky1 the rts5453 USB-PD controller can call
usb_role_switch_set_role() in that window, and cdns_role_stop() then
dereferences cdns->roles[role] == NULL (oops at offset 0x28, ->state).

Return early when the role driver is not registered yet.

Local workaround (BOOKWORM Sky1 kernel builder) - not an upstream patch.
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
@@ -59,6 +59,10 @@ static void cdns_role_stop(struct cdns *cdns)
 	if (WARN_ON(role > USB_ROLE_DEVICE))
 		return;
 
+	/* roles[] is populated after the role switch is registered */
+	if (!cdns->roles[role])
+		return;
+
 	if (cdns->roles[role]->state == CDNS_ROLE_STATE_INACTIVE)
 		return;
 
